@@ -9,6 +9,23 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## SMS verification setup
+
+Sign-up now requests a six-digit SMS code before creating the account. Configure these environment variables in the Node server environment (never expose them with a `PUBLIC_` prefix):
+
+```text
+TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=your-account-sid
+TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your-auth-token
+TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=your-SMS-capable-Twilio-number
+SMS_OTP_HOSTNAME=your-public-hostname.example
+```
+
+`SMS_OTP_HOSTNAME` must match the hostname users visit, without a scheme, port, or path. It defaults to the hostname in `astro.config.mjs`'s `site`. Serve the deployed page over HTTPS. Messages use a human-readable code followed by the final line `@hostname #code`, enabling origin-bound WebOTP and keyboard autofill. Delivery uses the [Twilio Messages API](https://www.twilio.com/docs/messaging/api/message-resource); provider credentials and an authorized SMS sender are required. No messages are sent during builds.
+
+The same-origin `api/signup` route verifies codes against the server session before calling the existing remote registration API. Codes expire after five minutes, permit five attempts, and are consumed on verification. Resending invalidates the earlier code. Each session permits one SMS request per minute and five per hour. A registration failure requires a fresh code; account details remain available for correction. Browsers without WebOTP retain keyboard autofill, paste, and manual entry.
+
+The Node adapter supplies filesystem session storage. Multi-instance deployments need a shared session driver and a shared atomic rate limiter keyed by phone/IP to enforce limits across sessions and concurrent requests. The separately hosted registration service remains independently reachable; enforcing verification for every API client requires updating that service to accept only trusted, verified registration requests. This repository gates its sign-up flow but cannot change that external service's policy.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
